id: hac-stpm
title: Unify typed service action execution across REST and WebSocket
description: "Provide a stable, type-safe, agent-oriented service action contract across Home Assistant REST and WebSocket transports, including response capability discovery, explicit targets, safe dry runs, strict validation, and normalized output."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 0
tags[8]: agents,api-parity,home-assistant,llm,rest,service-actions,type-safety,websocket
created_at: "2026-07-27T21:17:26.281Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-27T22:34:09.412Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-27T22:34:07.669Z"
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "call-service models current REST changed-state and service-response results plus WebSocket context/response results without any or guessed types; Agents can inspect and dry-run normalized requests, target selectors, transport choice, validation, and response capability before mutation; HASSIO_READONLY accepts explicit true and false values consistently through the complete Commander program; All source coverage and docstrings remain 100/100/100/100, every source file stays within 300 code lines, all formats and recursive help validate, and live evidence contains no private identifiers"
definition_of_ready: "Official REST and WebSocket docs, installed Commander/Undici types, live service schemas, prior PM lineage, and duplicate inventory reviewed"
goal: agent-safe-home-assistant-actions
objective: stable-cross-transport-service-execution
value: "Let agents plan, validate, execute, and interpret Home Assistant actions without transport-specific ambiguity."
impact: "Eliminates incorrectly typed REST results, improves target precision, prevents unsafe environment parsing surprises, and makes response-required services reliable."
outcome: One documented call-service workflow produces a stable envelope across REST and WebSocket and supports non-executing plans.
why_now: The current 2026.7.4 server exposes many response-capable actions and the official June 2026 REST contract no longer matches the CLI type; live ENV verification also found an explicit-false safety regression.
parent: hac-4s9j
reviewer: unbraind
risk: high
confidence: 94
sprint: api-parity-2026-07
release: unreleased
resolution: Delivered the normalized action platform and all acceptance evidence without publishing a package.
expected_result: "Production-ready typed Home Assistant service actions across REST and WebSocket with full safety, documentation, and verification."
actual_result: "Release verification, live Home Assistant acceptance, exact 100% coverage, privacy scans, CI, and review closure all pass."
